  "glow_note": "ItemObjectAttribute (ZzzObject.cpp:5238-5241): `case MODEL_STAFF_OF_RESURRECTION: BlendMesh = -2; BlendMeshLight = sin(WorldTime*0.004)*0.3 + 0.7` -- every mesh drawn added and breathing (ZzzBMD.cpp:1509) but mesh 2, wwe, which ZzzOpenData.cpp:1247 marks NoneBlendMesh: the red crystal stays solid, steel, and the rest glows about it.",
  "material_note": "wwe's red crystal facets are the one solid part, steel as the staves here; the other three are glows on MU's raw sheets.",
  "rig_note": "No .rig.json, on purpose, as Staff06: Staff07.bmd has seventeen bones and sixteen of them move through a 4-key action 0, which MuMain plays at fifteen times the stand's speed when held (ZzzCharacter.cpp:10125-10128); a held item is rigid here, so it is built at key 0 -- the .obj is MU's geometry posed there. Not here: the shimmer of its moving parts, and what MuMain hangs on it held -- a warm BITMAP_SPARK and a BITMAP_SHINY+2 at its head, 145 units up the hand, and four spark particles thrown about it each frame (ZzzCharacter.cpp:10302-10318), client effects.",
